/de7295fb1ce90f296716fd55780278163e28b4436a61efa8c146d230121ffe01" "q-91170/selection/3fa705e005f1c3a402401dbb9db6c250c1539dff933a18b4998905437c833187" "q-91170/selection/91302ed85ce211353d6918102cc72cc4238e71dd1b66a95d9a211f5b2429dc13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-91170" :question/id #uuid "5692854a-1edd-56c8-8906-b5a68a5133f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-91170" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{12}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries below ${a}_{12}=-1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}11 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}11 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91170/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfb