ual to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -2 & 12 \\\\ -7 & 2 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -11 & 4 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -11 & 4 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}-11 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3|\\begin{aligned}-11 & 4 & 10 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91166/selection/ma-v1/aff77b10136606220e2a2678ca2fa7356497f6cc7634451685b9809b6a703033"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169/selection/c9013ef8e694ecc23086db3bef02160a07bff663bbbf2942c1fc743e7d93c134" :answer/id #uuid "37d8c8bf-57e9-5f84-859a-1f71afaf98c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169/selection/c7731f2d916a2128600be9de2aca6b25ed23ca3c52c56174b79d7749122c673a" :answer/id #uuid "0d05fa6c-05d7-5999-a595-5233cb55367f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 16\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169/selection/d57082654a500ed722a3c5a3e7aeb42bc336110af796fa97d74a9771e6a679ae" :answer/id #uuid "aac7db63-f304-54dc-86bf-03651972d48d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169/selection/cf2d8db58efc035f1a1165aab91807fc9f0a9e6cbaf9141ed16dfec5c93fc874" :answer/id #uuid "b94465e2-29ca-56f2-b9b4-dafe7d7e5234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169/selection/a460c1a189b63aa71ccc1fcf6158fbe25970e6cea01012d670b8278d35796330" :answer/id #uuid "d2d0a0e7-6c33-52ea-a67b-b6c874a0d4af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 6\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d7ddeb3-d17a-59df-b7b4-d9d3d3c49864" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-91169/selection/d57082654a500ed722a3c5a3e7aeb42bc336110af796fa97d74a9771e6a679ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-91169/selection/c9013ef8e694ecc23086db3bef02160a07bff663bbbf2942c1fc743e7d93c134" "q-91169/selection/c7731f2d916a2128600be9de2aca6b25ed23ca3c52c56174b79d7749122c673a" "q-91169/selection/d57082654a500ed722a3c5a3e7aeb42bc336110af796fa97d74a9771e6a679ae" "q-91169/selection/cf2d8db58efc035f1a1165aab91807fc9f0a9e6cbaf9141ed16dfec5c93fc874" "q-91169/selection/a460c1a189b63aa71ccc1fcf6158fbe25970e6cea01012d670b8278d35796330"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-91169" :question/id #uuid "ef6e2c2f-2598-5c84-a9f7-82fa31430417" :question/math-academy-id "q-91169" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{23}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{23}=-2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 0 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 0 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 0 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 11 & 9 & 26 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91169/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-91169"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-91196/selection/fa77cc6436f8d62c869e59f887e1435d8db50a9dda7919462eac1cbe953ff194" :answer/id #uuid "3c93ccd5-99ce-5dd3-9601-bc1f2513f701" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91196/selection/101cd2ee76e6d5922a4e16280fe2e7d6510c8aadca983fa68d74581faf405370" :answer/id #uuid "be9005ee-5494-52ab-8266-15c965d513db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91196/selection/a5b6d39949c0fffa830eae112fac9139733e18720fbed6464b352b23cf1c5f87" :answer/id #